    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d285">

                <pb facs="0557" n="423" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg423"/>

                <head>No. 285.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Walker.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-06"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 6,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of a letter from Mr. Leonard
                    Myers, of Philadelphia, relating to the claim of the Panama Star and Herald
                    against the Government of Colombia.<anchor n="*" xml:id="d285-f1"/></p>
                <p>As this case does not fall within the lines of the negotiations begun some time
                    ago in reference to the settlement of claims for destruction of property during
                    the disturbances on the Isthmus, it is hoped the Colombian Government will
                    consider and adjust the claim on its merits and without reference to the method
                    of disposing of other classes of claims.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d285-a1.xml" xpointer="d285-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d285-f1" n="*" xml:id="d285-f1-content">
                <p>For previous correspondence relative to the case of the Panama Star and Herald,
                    see <ref target="frus1886#pg_168">Foreign Relations 1886, pages 168</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1886#pg_176">176</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
